Subject: [PATCH 1/7] FlyWeb 3.2.0 interface: frame, toolbar, active tab and
 URL colors

Colors from Titin's design (softmac FlyWeb/branding/interfaz-3.2.0):
- Active tab and toolbar share one color: #F4F5F6 light, #656666 dark.
- Frame (bar of the inactive tabs): #E3E3E2 light, #4D4D4C dark, also
  for windows without focus.
- URL field: white in both modes.

In dark mode the URL field and the suggestion popup are both white with
dark text (kFlyWebLightOmniboxInDarkMode). Chromium paints the focused
field with the popup background and both share the text color ids, so
a white field needs a white popup. The CR2023 omnibox colors, built from
the dark-mode ui::kColorSys* tokens, are replaced by Chromium's own
contrast-based recipes so they follow the white backgrounds. Private and
Tor windows keep Brave's colors.

